Password Policy and Account Lockout Investigation
Objective
Configure password security requirements and investigate account lockout events within Active Directory.

Environment
Domain Controller
Windows Server 2022
Active Directory Domain Services
DNS Server
Client Workstation
Windows 11
Security Objectives
Enforce password requirements
Configure account lockout protections
Generate authentication failures
Investigate security events
Analyze logs using PowerShell
Actions Performed
Password Policy
Configured a minimum password length of 12 characters.

Account Lockout Policy
Configured account lockout after 5 failed login attempts.

Authentication Testing
Generated failed logins against a domain account to trigger account lockout protections.

Security Investigation
Reviewed Windows Security Event Logs to identify authentication failures.

PowerShell Audit
Queried Event ID 4625 events using PowerShell.

Findings
The configured account lockout policy successfully disabled access after multiple failed login attempts.

Authentication failures generated Event ID 4625 entries within the Windows Security Log.

PowerShell was able to retrieve and export authentication failure events for analysis.

Skills Demonstrated
Active Directory Administration
Group Policy Management
Security Monitoring
Event Viewer Analysis
PowerShell Administration
Incident Investigation
Windows Server Administration
Lessons Learned
Password policies and account lockout controls provide an important layer of protection against password guessing attacks. Windows Event Viewer and PowerShell can be used together to investigate authentication failures and security events.
